    "guest": "Саша"
  },
  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "In a brief moment of chaos, Max realizes he needs to take control of a difficult situation. He tells his colleagues that they will figure it out and urges them to go. Let us listen to their conversation in Russian first.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ладно, мы разберёмся с этим.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Всё будет хорошо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Что нам делать сейчас?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Поехали.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Куда мы едем?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мы никуда не едем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это значит, что мы начинаем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Теперь я всё понял.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Тогда давайте работать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, за работу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "У нас мало времени.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Мы должны успеть.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Конечно мы успеем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Тогда начинаем прямо сейчас.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let us examine the conversation line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ладно, мы разберёмся с этим.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Alright, we will figure this out.' The reflexive ending on the verb for 'will sort this out' turns the action back onto the subject.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Всё будет хорошо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Everything will be fine.' Notice the word order: 'will be' comes first, and 'good' finishes the sentence. Ilya answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Что нам делать сейчас?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What should we do now?' Here 'what' sets up the idea, while 'now' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Поехали.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Let's go.' You'll hear 'here we go' all the time in the show, here connected with 'here we go'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Куда мы едем?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Where are we going?' The key word here means 'where to', which Sasha combines with 'we'. Then Max replies.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мы никуда не едем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We are not going anywhere.' Max starts with 'we' and pairs it with 'nowhere' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это значит, что мы начинаем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It means that we are starting.' Max puts 'this' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'then'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Теперь я всё понял.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Now I understand everything.' In Russian, 'now' leads into 'understood?' in a very natural everyday phrasing. And Sasha jumps in.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Тогда давайте работать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Then let's work.' The key word here means 'back then', which Sasha combines with 'let's'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, за работу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, back to work.' A compact expression built around 'job' and 'job'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "У нас мало времени.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We have little time.' Ilya starts with 'us' and pairs it with 'little' to make the point clear. Sasha answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Мы должны успеть.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We must be in time.' Notice the word order: 'we' comes first, and 'to make it' finishes the sentence.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Конечно мы успеем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Of course we will be in time.' Listen for the word meaning 'of course' right alongside 'we' in this line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Тогда начинаем прямо сейчас.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Then we start right now.' The first content word means 'back then', and 'now' rounds out the thought. Now let us listen to the conversation once again.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
